 ex:l6s-d-41 a cd:TableCell ; cd:position 1 ; cd:body "0.8 or more"@en . ex:l6s-d-42 a cd:TableCell ; cd:position 2 ; cd:body "Large"@en .
 ex:l6s-lake-art a cd:MediaAsset ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level6-lake-comic.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Two comic panels compare conservative and progressive GO decisions. True thickness 10.3 cm: GO 32.8% versus 99.8%. True thickness 9.7 cm: GO 0.22% versus 67.2%. These are repeated-study decision rates in a thickness-only model."@en .
 ex:l6s-lake-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:bodyFormat "markdown" ; cd:body "**Severe consequences of a false GO: require evidence before acting. A progressive rule needs an explicit, acceptable error-cost trade-off.**"@en .
 ex:l6s-multi-art a cd:MediaAsset ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level6-three-analytes.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "One water sample supplies independent replicate preparations. Each preparation is analysed for chloride, bromate and phosphate. Three population mean claims compare each analyte with its own limit. Shared preparation errors can link analytes."@en .
 ex:l6s-independence-setup a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Show experiment: rows and columns"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level6-independence-setup.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Forty independent vessels: twenty control, twenty exposure. One affected/unaffected classification per vessel. Rows encode group; columns encode classification. Observed counts 8/12 and 14/6 give row totals 20/20, column totals 22/18, grand total 40."@en .
 ex:l6s-pair-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Build U: compare one pair, score it, add the points"@en .
 ex:l6s-pair-animation a cd:ChartDefinition ; cd:chartType cd:ScientificExperiment ; cd:experimentKind "pairwise-score" ; skos:prefLabel "Pairwise score account"@en ; cd:body "- Keep the original X and Y identities.\n- Compare every cross-group pair once.\n- X greater: +1; tie: +0.5; X smaller: +0."@en ; cd:xAxisLabel "Comparison"@en ; cd:yAxisLabel "Score account U_X"@en ; cd:usesDataset ex:l6s-pair-data ; cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:l6s-pair-step .
 ex:l6s-pair-step a cd:ExperimentParameter ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Completed comparisons"@en ; cd:parameterKey "step" ; cd:numericValue 0.0 ; cd:parameterMinimum 0.0 ; cd:parameterMaximum 9.0 ; cd:parameterStep 1.0 ; cd:adjustableParameter true .
 ex:l6s-pair-data a cd:Dataset ; cd:hasObservation ex:l6s-x1, ex:l6s-x2, ex:l6s-x3, ex:l6s-y1, ex:l6s-y2, ex:l6s-y3 .
 ex:l6s-x1 a cd:Observation ; cd:position 1 ; cd:numericValue 1.0 ; cd:pairedValue 0.0 ; skos:prefLabel "X₁"@en .
 ex:l6s-x2 a cd:Observation ; cd:position 2 ; cd:numericValue 2.0 ; cd:pairedValue 0.0 ; skos:prefLabel "X₂"@en .
 ex:l6s-x3 a cd:Observation ; cd:position 3 ; cd:numericValue 2.0 ; cd:pairedValue 0.0 ; skos:prefLabel "X₃"@en .
 ex:l6s-y1 a cd:Observation ; cd:position 4 ; cd:numericValue 2.0 ; cd:pairedValue 1.0 ; skos:prefLabel "Y₁"@en .
 ex:l6s-y2 a cd:Observation ; cd:position 5 ; cd:numericValue 3.0 ; cd:pairedValue 1.0 ; skos:prefLabel "Y₂"@en .
 ex:l6s-y3 a cd:Observation ; cd:position 6 ; cd:numericValue 4.0 ; cd:pairedValue 1.0 ; skos:prefLabel "Y₃"@en .
 ex:l6s-u-reference-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "From U = 1 to p = 0.300: relabel the six observations"@en .
 ex:l6s-u-reference a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6s-u-a, ex:l6s-u-b .
 ex:l6s-u-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "20 EQUALLY LIKELY LABEL ASSIGNMENTS UNDER H₀"@en ; cd:body "- **H₀:** equal distributions; independent observations with exchangeable group labels.\n- Choose **3 of 6** original observations for X: **20** assignments. Tied observations retain their identities.\n- Recalculate **U** for every assignment. The null centre is **4.5**."@en .
 ex:l6s-u-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "COUNT BOTH EXTREMES"@en ; cd:body "- Observed **U = 1** lies **3.5** from the centre.\n- **U ≤ 1 or U ≥ 8:** six of twenty assignments are at least this far away.\n- **p = 6/20 = 0.300 > 0.05:** do not reject H₀. This is a declared tie-aware, two-sided permutation reference."@en .
 ex:l6s-sign-reference-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Five differences, 32 sign patterns: where does p come from?"@en .
 ex:l6s-sign-reference a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6s-sign-a, ex:l6s-sign-b .
 ex:l6s-sign-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "TWO POSSIBLE SIGNS FOR EACH ORIGINAL DIFFERENCE"@en ; cd:body "- Keep absolute differences **1, 2, 3, 4, 5 µg/L** and their ranks fixed.\n- Under the symmetric zero-shift **H₀**, each independent sign is equally likely **+ or −**.\n- Five binary choices give **2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 = 32** sign patterns."@en .
 ex:l6s-sign-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "THE TWO-SIDED TAILS"@en ; cd:body "- Observed positive-rank sum **W⁺ = 13**; total rank sum **15**, centre **7.5**.\n- At least as extreme: **W⁺ ≤ 2 or W⁺ ≥ 13**. Three patterns in each tail.\n- **p = (3 + 3)/32 = 0.1875**. At 5%, do not reject the zero-shift H₀."@en .
 ex:l6s-effect-interpretation a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6s-effect-reading .
 ex:l6s-effect-reading a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "OUR RESULT: d = −1.677"@en ; cd:body "- **Sign:** NIR reads lower than HPLC-MS in this comparison.\n- **Magnitude:** the mean difference is about **1.68 pooled within-group SDs**.\n- **|d| = 1.677:** **large** by the conventional bands. Assess chemical relevance using the application."@en .
 ex:l6s-esd-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Several suspected outliers? Plan a multiple-outlier procedure"@en .
 ex:l6s-esd a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6s-esd-a, ex:l6s-esd-b .
 ex:l6s-esd-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "GENERALIZED ESD"@en ; cd:body "- Set an **upper bound r** on the suspected outlier count **before testing**.\n- Calculate successive extreme-deviation statistics with **ESD's adjusted cutoffs**.\n- Use the **largest qualifying step**. Background model: **approximately Normal**."@en .
 ex:l6s-esd-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "REPEATED GRUBBS OR BONFERRONI?"@en ; cd:body "- Fresh unadjusted 5% tests change error behaviour; extremes can **mask** one another.\n- A simple **Bonferroni adjustment** alone does not resolve adaptive deletion and masking.\n- NIST approximation: **reasonable n ≥ 15**, **stronger n ≥ 25**. Our **n = 6** example remains single-outlier Grubbs."@en .
}

